<%# Session detail page. The body lives in the shared _detail partial so it can
    also be lazy-loaded into the dashboard's right-side drawer.

    Two actions render this template, and which one you are in is decided by the
    URL, never by a request header: #show (/sessions/:id) renders the full page
    without a frame, so internal Turbo navigations still target _top, and #drawer
    (/sessions/:id/drawer) wraps the same body in <turbo-frame id="session_detail">
    and renders chrome-light so it swaps cleanly into the drawer panel. Keeping the
    two bodies on disjoint URLs is what stops a URL-keyed cache — Turbo's prefetch
    cache above all — from serving the frameless one to the drawer's frame request
    and leaving it showing "Content missing". See SessionsController#drawer. %>
<% if @in_drawer %>
  <%= turbo_frame_tag "session_detail" do %>
    <%= render "sessions/detail", in_drawer: true %>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <%= render "sessions/detail", in_drawer: false %>
<% end %>
